nuclear localization sequences on influenza a ribonucleoprotein complexes</article-title><source>J Mol Biol</source><year>2007</year><volume>374</volume><fpage>910</fpage><lpage>916</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17976646</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jmb.2007.10.022</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sidorenko</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Reichl</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Structured model of influenza virus replication in MDCK cells</article-title><source>Biotechnol Bioeng</source><year>2004</year><volume>88</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>14</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15384040</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/bit.20096</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boulo</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Akarsu</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruigrok</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>Baudin</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nuclear traffic of influenza virus proteins and ribonucleoprotein complexes</article-title><source>Virus Res</source><year>2007</year><volume>124</volume><fpage>12</fpage><lpage>21</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17081640</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.virusres.2006.09.013</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Elton</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Simpson-Holley</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Archer</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Medcalf</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Hallam</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>McCa